{"name":"Stomy Shower","hex":"#0088b0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brief fall of precipitation (spell of rain, or a similar fall of snow, sleet, or cascade); burst of hefty precipitation.","A device for bathing by which water is made to fall on the body from a height, either from a tank or by the action of a pump."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spray with (a specified liquid) .","To bathe using a shower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stoma (medicine)","blocks":[{"text":"In anatomy, a stoma is any opening in the body. For example, a mouth, a nose, and an anus are natural stomata. Any hollow organ can be manipulated into an artificial stoma as necessary. This includes the esophagus, stomach, duodenum, ileum, colon, pleural cavity, ureters, urinary bladder, and renal pelvis. Such a stoma may be permanent or temporary."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoma_(medicine)"},{"title":"Shower","blocks":[{"text":"A shower is a place in which a person bathes under a spray of typically warm or hot water. Indoors, there is a drain in the floor. Most showers are set up to have adjustable temperature, spray pressure, and showerhead nozzle angle. The simplest showers have a swivelling nozzle aimed downward, while more complex showers have a showerhead connected to a hose that has a mounting bracket; this allows the showerer to hold the showerhead by hand to spray the water onto different parts of their body. A showerhead can be installed in a small shower stall or bathtub, with a plastic shower curtain or door."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/IMG_Duschender.jpg/330px-IMG_Duschender.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shower"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Colostomie.jpg/500px-Colostomie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Colostomie.jpg/1280px-Colostomie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Colostomie.jpg/500px-Colostomie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Colostomy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColostomie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG/500px-Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG/1280px-Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG/500px-Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Patient with a colostomy complicated by a large parastomal hernia, which is when tissue protrudes adjacent to the stoma tract.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColostomy_and_parastomal_hernia.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia_-_CT.png/500px-Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia_-_CT.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia_-_CT.png/500px-Colostomy_and_parastomal_hernia_-_CT.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"CT scan of same patient, showing intestines within the hernia.\nParastomal hernia is the most common late complication of stomata through the abdominal wall, occurring in 10 to 25% of the patients.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColostomy_and_parastomal_hernia_-_CT.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg/250px-Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg/250px-Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A typical stall shower with height-adjustable nozzle and folding doors","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Badewanne_%28fcm%29.jpg/500px-Badewanne_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Badewanne_%28fcm%29.jpg/500px-Badewanne_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A combination shower and bathtub, with movable screen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABadewanne_(fcm).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/The_Douche._Wellcome_L0003967.jpg/500px-The_Douche._Wellcome_L0003967.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/The_Douche._Wellcome_L0003967.jpg/1280px-The_Douche._Wellcome_L0003967.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/The_Douche._Wellcome_L0003967.jpg/500px-The_Douche._Wellcome_L0003967.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of showers from T